
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.LinksetDataListKeys(start: number, count: number): {any}`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`list llLinksetDataListKeys(integer start, integer count);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>The <b>llLinksetDataListKeys</b> function returns a list of up to <b>count</b> keys in the datastore, starting at the one indicated by <b>start</b>. If <b>count</b> is less than 1, then all keys between <b>start</b> and the end are returned. If <b>count</b> minus <b>start</b> exceeds the total number of keys, the returned list will be shorter than <b>count</b>, down to a zero-length list if <b>start</b> equals or exceeds the total number of keys.</p>
  <p>Returns a list of the keys in the datastore, ordered alphabetically.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>number</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>integer</span></td>
          <td>start</td>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>It's 1 based</span>The first key to return.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>number</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>integer</span></td>
          <td>count</td>
          <td>The number of keys to return.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>data_storage</li>
        <li>linkset</li>
        <li>linkset_data</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">656</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-mandatory">Use Return</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
  <p>The following code will list all the keys in a object. Only 1024 characters will be displayed due to limitations of <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSay" target="_blank">llSay</a>.</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

-- Retrieving too many entries from LinksetData can trigger a stack or heap error if the number of entries exceeds the available memory.  Use with caution.

local function main()
    ll.Say(0, ll.DumpList2String(ll.LinksetDataListKeys(0, 0), "\n"))
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// Retrieving too many entries from LinksetData can trigger a stack or heap error if the number of entries exceeds the available memory.  Use with caution.

default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llSay(0, llDumpList2String(llLinksetDataListKeys(0, 0), "\n"));
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
